course: dictionary
lesson: 730
title: A baseline is a starting line
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A baseline is a starting point, a line you measure from or stand behind. The word has two parts: base means the bottom or start, and line is a line. «The line letters sit on is the baseline.» So the baseline is the line that letters rest on when you write.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence: «Tall parts of letters (b, d, h) are ascenders; tails below the line (g, p, y) are descenders; the line letters sit on is the baseline.» Ascenders go up above the line, descenders hang down below it, and the baseline is the line in between. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Baseline can also mean a measurement taken at the start. Scientists measure before they change anything, so they can see how much things changed later. A «baseline test» shows what a pupil knows at the start of the year. In tennis, players serve from behind the baseline, the line at the back of the court.
fact: A baseline is the line that letters sit on when you write.
fact: Tall letters like b, d and h go above the baseline, and letters like g, p and y have tails that go below it.
fact: A baseline is also a starting measurement, taken before anything changes, so you can compare later results with it.
fact: In tennis, the baseline is the line at the back of each end of the court.
fact: A baseline can also mean a basic level, such as the lowest acceptable standard.
exercise: «Tall parts of letters (b, d, h) are ascenders; tails below the line (g, p, y) are descenders.» Which letter has a tail that goes below the baseline? | d | *g | h | b
exercise: A scientist measures a plant's height before she changes anything. Why is this measurement called a baseline? | *It is the starting measurement, to compare later results with | It is the tallest result of the whole experiment | It is the line at the back of the court | It is the last measurement, taken after everything has changed
exercise: «In tennis, players serve from behind the ___.» Which word fits the gap? | side | *baseline | net | service box
test: A «baseline test» at the start of the year shows what a pupil already knows. What does it show? | Who won last year's race | How fast a pupil can run | *What a pupil already knows at the start | The best day to go on holiday
test: Ascenders are the tall parts of letters. Which letter has an ascender? | y | g | *h | p
exam: Which meaning fits baseline best when it means a starting measurement? | *The starting point you compare later results with | A type of holiday | A long, thin cloud | A kind of tennis racket
